-- title:
--   Local Borel frame for an Eichler suborder at p ∥ N
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project: $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is the whole algebra, and $R$ is finitely generated. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $p$ a prime number whose image in $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the ideal of $w$; write $\mathbb{Q}_w$ for the $w$-adic completion and $\mathcal{O}_w$ for its valuation subring. Let $\varphi_w:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\xrightarrow{\sim}M_2(\mathbb{Q}_w)$ be a ring isomorphism with $\varphi_w(1\otimes c)=c\cdot 1$ for all $c\in\mathbb{Q}_w$, and let $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_w)$ be such that the local box of $R$ at $w$ — the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c\in\mathcal{O}_w$ — consists exactly of those $x$ with all entries of $h^{-1}\varphi_w(x)h$ in $\mathcal{O}_w$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $p\mid N$ and $p^2\nmid N$, and let $\varphi:R\to M_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-linear, sending $1$ to $1$, satisfying $\varphi(xy)=\varphi(x)\varphi(y)$ for $x,y\in R$, surjective, and with $\varphi(x)=0$ if and only if $x=N\cdot y$ for some $y\in R$. Let $R_0$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule contained in $R$ such that, for $x\in R$, membership $x\in R_0$ is equivalent to $\varphi(x)_{1,0}=0$. Then there exists $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_w)$ such that the local box of $R$ at $w$ is again the set of $x$ with $g^{-1}\varphi_w(x)g\in M_2(\mathcal{O}_w)$, and the local box of $R_0$ at $w$ is the set of $x$ such that both $g^{-1}\varphi_w(x)g$ and $\operatorname{diag}(1,p^{-1})\,g^{-1}\varphi_w(x)g\,\operatorname{diag}(1,p)$ have all entries in $\mathcal{O}_w$.
--
--   This produces a single local frame at $w$ in which the completion of $R$ is the standard maximal order $M_2(\mathcal{O}_w)$ and the completion of the suborder $R_0$ cut out by the lower-left entry of the mod-$N$ reduction is the standard Eichler order of level $p$, written as the intersection of $M_2(\mathcal{O}_w)$ with its $\operatorname{diag}(1,p)$-conjugate. It feeds the construction of a maximal order together with an Eichler suborder having prescribed local boxes, used in the quaternionic side of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_localBox_iff_and_localBox_iff_conj_diagonal_of_linearMap_matrix_zmod.lean

